<title>SOUTH AFRICA: South African Oct new car sales up 28.4 percent yr/yr.</title>
<headline>South African Oct new car sales up 28.4 percent yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African new car sales rose 28.4 percent to 27,816 units in October from 19,927 units in September and 21,662 units in the same month a year ago, latest National Association of Automobile Manufacturers of South Africa figures show.</p>
<p>Monthly sales were at the highest since June 1982, when 28,507 units were sold, NAAMSA said.</p>
<p>    Detailed Sales data:	   Oct  96 Sep 96  Oct  95</p>
<p>    New passenger cars	     27,816  19,927  21,662</p>
<p>    Light commercial vehicles    12,158  10,256  11,762</p>
<p>    Medium commercial vehicles   665     513     391</p>
<p>    Heavy commercial vehicles    740     638     794</p>
<p>    TOTAL:			     41,379  31,334  34,609</p>
<p>Individual manufacturer car sales:</p>
<p>Toyota 6,650, Volkswagen 6,755, Samcor 5,454, Nissan 3,112, Delta 1,458, Mercedes-Benz 2,227, BMW 1,612, Land Rover SA 171, Daewoo 368, Dacia 2, Subaru 7.</p>
<p>					    Jan-Oct  96   Jan-Oct  95</p>
<p>    New passenger cars		208,483	 199,285</p>
<p>    Light commercial vehicles     110,245	 108,731</p>
<p>    Medium commercial vehicles	4,609	   3,521</p>
<p>    Heavy commercial vehicles	 6,954	   6,553</p>
<p>    TOTAL:				330,291	 318,090</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
